# =============================================================================
#  CUI-CPP.orch - Company Performance Prediction (MPAI-CUI, CPP V2.1)
#  Workflow Description Language v0.3, AIF V3.0
#
#  The same workflow for the console App (CuiUa) and for the MAS App. One Controller, one Module -
#  Company Performance Prediction, 1CUI-CPP-V2.1-I01 - which executes continuously: its AIMs feed one
#  another, and what one gives another is the Topology's business, never the User Agent's. The User
#  Agent knows the Module's boundary only, by Data Type and Port Number:
#
#    what is given -
#      Financial (CUI-FND)               the Financial Descriptors of the company
#      Governance (CUI-GVS)              its Governance Descriptors
#      Climate (CUI-LRD)                 its Climate Risk Descriptors                       (optional)
#      Cyber (CUI-CRD)                   its Cyber Risk Descriptors                         (optional)
#      SecondaryRisks (CUI-SRS)          its Secondary Risk Statements                      (optional)
#      Horizon (number)                  the Prediction Horizon, in months
#
#    what the Module gives -
#      Organisation (CUI-ORD)            what the organisation does to the probability of default
#      PrimaryDefault (CUI-PDD)          the probability of default within the Horizon, and the weight of each figure
#      PrimaryDiscontinuity (CUI-PSD)    the probability that operations are interrupted, by risk
#      SecondaryProbability (number)     the Secondary Discontinuity Probability            (only with SecondaryRisks)
#
#  THE COMPANY. A device "Company" gives the Module what the person chooses, as they choose it: a company -
#  ready-made (the App's files: companies/index.json names them in plain words) or a file of their own in the
#  format of the App's README - part by part (a part the company does not have is not given), the Prediction
#  Horizon, and, after a result, the WHAT-IF: five figures of the same company moved (revenues, operating
#  result, total debts, equity, financial expenses) - the device changes the Financial Descriptors it holds
#  and gives them again; the Module computes again on the new input. No AIM is touched.
#  THE RESULTS are delivered to a device "Report" as the Module gives them: its AIMs compute again whenever
#  an input changes, so the Report keeps the latest of each and shows them as they come.
# =============================================================================

workflow CUI-CPP over 1CUI-CPP-V2.1-I01

on Start:

    ask Controller to start

    stream  Horizon               (number)        from device "Company"
    stream  Financial             (CUI-FND-V2.1)  from device "Company"
    stream  Governance            (CUI-GVS-V2.1)  from device "Company"
    stream  Climate               (CUI-LRD-V2.1)  from device "Company"
    stream  Cyber                 (CUI-CRD-V2.1)  from device "Company"
    stream  SecondaryRisks        (CUI-SRS-V2.1)  from device "Company"

    deliver Organisation          (CUI-ORD-V2.1)  to device "Report"
    deliver PrimaryDefault        (CUI-PDD-V2.1)  to device "Report"
    deliver PrimaryDiscontinuity  (CUI-PSD-V2.1)  to device "Report"
    deliver SecondaryProbability  (number)        to device "Report"

    prompt "Company Performance Prediction tells how likely a company is to default, or to stop operating, within a horizon of 12, 24 or 36 months, and why: which of its figures weigh most. The model is a demonstration, trained on Polish companies: it is not for real decisions. Choose a company, ready-made or a file of your own, and the horizon; then move a figure and see what changes."

    loop until Stop:
        wait 1s

on Stop:
    ask Controller to stop
